design VeerFlow UX model (navigation, layout, interaction)

Let’s design VeerFlow as a first-class interaction system, not a skinned browser.
Think: command + canvas + live system—all in one.

🧠 0. Design Principles (non-negotiable)
Invoke-first — everything starts from intent (invoke()), not location

Live by default — no refresh; all views are streams

Identity-native — permissions shape what you see/do

Composable — views are assembled, not loaded

Context-preserving — navigation never “loses state”

Zero chrome — UI disappears when not needed

🧭 1. Navigation Model — Intent, not URLs
🔹 Command Palette = Primary Entry
Open with a single key (like ⌘K):

auth.login
user.profile id=123
analytics.dashboard region=apac
autocomplete from fabric namespace

shows permissions inline

executes immediately or opens a view

👉 This replaces:

address bar

bookmarks

most menus

🔹 Semantic Navigation
navigate("workspace.analytics")
navigate("user.profile", { id: 123 })
routes are namespaced functions/views

parameters are explicit (no query-string hacks)

🔹 Context Stack (not tabs)
Instead of tabs, you get a stack of contexts:

[Home] → [Analytics] → [User 123] → [Payment Detail]
swipe/gesture to move back/forward

each context keeps its live state

branching allowed (like git branches of UI)

👉 No reloads, no lost scroll, no re-fetch

🧩 2. Layout Model — Canvas + Panels
🔹 The Canvas
A flexible, zoomable workspace where views live

infinite canvas (pan/zoom)

multiple views side-by-side

drag to arrange

🔹 View = First-Class Object
view("analytics.summary", {
  data: invoke("analytics.summary"),
  streams: [subscribe("alerts.stream")]
})
A view has:

data bindings (invoke)

live streams (subscribe)

actions (invoke again)

🔹 Layout Primitives
1. Tiles
standard panels (tables, charts, logs)

2. Stacks
layered views (like drill-down)

3. Split Views
compare or monitor multiple contexts

4. Overlays
transient actions (forms, alerts)

🔹 Example Layout
+-------------------+-------------------+
| Analytics Summary | Live Alerts       |
| (charts)          | (stream)          |
+-------------------+-------------------+
| User Activity Feed (real-time)        |
+--------------------------------------+
👉 Everything updates live, no refresh

⚡ 3. Interaction Model — Direct + Reactive
🔹 Actions = Invoke
Buttons don’t call APIs—they invoke functions:

onClick → invoke("payment.refund", { id })
immediate feedback via event stream

optimistic UI possible

🔹 Data = Subscriptions
subscribe("orders.stream")
UI updates as events arrive

no polling, no manual refresh

🔹 Inline Editing (No Forms Pages)
click any field → edit inline

commit triggers invoke()

Name: [John Doe] → edit → save → invoke("user.update")
🔹 Multi-Select + Batch Actions
select multiple items

apply function once

invoke("user.disable", { ids: [...] })
🔄 4. State & Time Model — Time Travel UI
🔹 Timeline Slider
Every view can:

rewind state

replay events

Now ◀──────────────▶ Past
👉 Debugging becomes visual

🔹 Snapshots
save a state of the canvas

shareable with others

🧠 5. Identity-Aware UX
🔹 UI Adapts to Permissions
unavailable actions are hidden (not just disabled)

data visibility filtered at source

🔹 Trust Indicators
each view shows:

data source (fabric)

trust level

policy context

🔔 6. Notifications → Event Streams
No popups. Instead:

Notification Stream Panel

filterable by:

severity

source

function

[ALERT] auth failures spike
[INFO ] deployment complete
🔍 7. Search = System Query
Search is not text—it’s structured:

errors last:5m
payments status=failed region=eu
👉 Queries the Console Fabric

🧪 8. Developer Mode (Built-in)
Toggle “Dev Mode”:

see raw events

inspect invokes

trace execution path

invoke → node → latency → result
👉 No external tools needed

🧠 9. Mental Model Shift
❌ Old (Browser)
Page → Load → Call APIs → Render → Refresh
✅ VeerFlow
View → Bind → Stream → React → Evolve
🔥 10. Signature UX Moments
These define VeerFlow:

1. “Everything is live”
numbers change in front of you

2. “No loading screens”
skeleton → instant streaming

3. “Command + Visual unity”
type OR click—same system

4. “System-wide awareness”
you see across nodes, not one app

🧩 11. Minimal Visual Language
dark-first (system feel)

neon accents (events, alerts)

subtle motion (flow of data)

🚀 12. Final Definition
VeerFlow is a live, identity-aware, invocation-driven interaction layer for the fabric—where UI is composed of streaming views bound directly to execution and state.

