Perfect—this is the piece that turns VeerFlow from concept into something you can actually build.

We’ll design the VeerFlow Client Runtime (VFCR) as a local, secure, event-driven engine that sits between UI and the fabric.

🧠 0. Core Responsibility
The client runtime is a mini fabric node on the user device, specialized for interaction.

It must handle:

identity

invocation

streaming state

UI execution

policy enforcement

offline behavior

🧱 1. High-Level Architecture
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                VeerFlow UI                   │
│        (Views / Components / Canvas)         │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│          View Runtime (UI Engine)            │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Invocation Engine  |  State Sync Engine      │
│ Event Engine       |  Policy Engine          │
